```
- Appending from file and then appending from scene also triggers `ERR_CONTINUE(!mi);` (otherwise it works correctly, checked by `write_to_filesystem`). Example code:
```
	var gltf := GLTFDocument.new()
	var gltf_state := GLTFState.new()
	gltf.append_from_file("res://test.gltf", gltf_state, 0, 0)
	gltf.append_from_scene(self, gltf_state, 0, 0)
```
- Appending from scene and then appending from file results in many `ERR_CONTINUE(state->nodes[child_i]->parent != -1);` on `_parse_nodes` (it works, but it seems to cause some extra duplicates, keeping in mind I'm using an gltf form a similar version of the scene). Example code:
```
	var gltf := GLTFDocument.new()
	var gltf_state := GLTFState.new()
	gltf.append_from_scene(self, gltf_state, 0, 0)
	gltf.append_from_file("res://test.gltf", gltf_state, 0, 0)
```
- Appending buffers twice (the same or different) also triggers many `ERR_CONTINUE(state->nodes[child_i]->parent != -1);` (there seems to be three copies in the result, instead of two). Example code:
```
	var gltf := GLTFDocument.new()
	var gltf_state := GLTFState.new()
	var gltf_state_2 := GLTFState.new()
	gltf.append_from_scene(self, gltf_state, 0, 0)
	var b = gltf.generate_buffer(gltf_state)
	gltf.append_from_buffer(b, "", 0, 0, gltf_state_2)
	gltf.append_from_buffer(b, "", 0, 0, gltf_state_2)
```
- Also appending from file twice (they can be the same file or not) triggers many `ERR_CONTINUE(state->nodes[child_i]->parent != -1);` (otherwise it works correctly). Example code:
```
	var gltf := GLTFDocument.new()
